    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <div class="faq"><h3>How much does a dog cost per year?</h3><p>A small dog costs $1,390-$2,000 per year. A medium dog runs $2,100-$3,200. A large dog can cost $3,000-$5,295 annually. First year costs are always higher due to spay/neuter, supplies, and training.</p></div>
    <div class="faq"><h3>How much does a cat cost per year?</h3><p>Cats typically cost $760-$1,500 per year for food, vet care, litter, and supplies. First year costs are higher - expect $1,750-$2,200 including spay/neuter and initial setup.</p></div>
    <div class="faq"><h3>Is pet insurance worth it?</h3><p>Pet insurance makes financial sense if your pet needs surgery or chronic care. A single emergency visit averages $800-$1,500. Insurance runs $350-$1,100 per year depending on pet and coverage level.</p></div>
    <div class="faq"><h3>What is the lifetime cost of a pet?</h3><p>A medium dog costs around $34,000 over 12 years. A cat costs $20,000-$32,000 over 16 years. Most owners predict far less - the gap between predicted and actual is the biggest financial surprise in pet ownership.</p></div>
    <div class="faq"><h3>What costs do first-time pet owners miss?</h3><p>The most commonly missed costs are boarding/pet sitting ($300-$700/yr), grooming ($200-$500/yr), dental cleanings ($500-$1,000), and emergency vet care. Budget a separate $2,000-$5,000 emergency fund.</p></div>
